# Bilingual Workflow (EM III Accompany)

This project supports **international students** in Advanced Econometrics. Use a strict language split.

## Conversation → Chinese (中文)

- The user may ask in **中文**; **reply in 中文** for explanations, summaries, questions, and status updates.
- Do not switch chat language to English unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Project Artifacts → English

All student-facing and repository content must be **English**:

| Applies to | Examples |
|------------|----------|
| Quarto / Markdown | `index.qmd`, `menu/*.qmd`, `README.md` — titles, headings, body text, callouts |
| R code | comments, variable labels, plot axes, `DT` captions, `kable` titles |
| Config | `_quarto.yml` navbar/sidebar labels, YAML `title` / `subtitle` |
| Data labels | `.txt` label files, exported table headers |
| Git | commit messages and PR text (English unless user asks otherwise) |

## Editing Rules

1. **New content** — write in English from the start.
2. **Existing Chinese content** — translate to English as part of the edit; avoid leaving mixed-language student-facing text.
3. **LaTeX / math** — standard econometrics notation (IV, 2SLS, TSLS, SEM, OLS); prose around formulas stays English.
4. **Chat vs files** — explain changes in 中文 in chat; never put 中文 explanations into project files unless the user explicitly requests bilingual artifacts.

## Quick Examples

```
User: 请更新 index.qmd 的介绍
→ Reply in 中文; rewrite index.qmd body in English

User: 给 code-mroz.R 加注释
→ Reply in 中文; comments in English: # Fit first-stage regression

User: 侧边栏加一个 SEM 页面
→ Reply in 中文; _quarto.yml text: "SEM Application"; page content in English
```
